From: vcpkg migration
Subject: [PATCH] Use the dlopen-based loader even for a static libwpe

libwpe selects src/loader-static.c when default_library != 'shared'. The
static loader references an external `_wpe_loader_interface` struct that a
backend statically linked into the final binary is expected to provide. In
the OpenHarmony build libwpe is built static (so it folds into the shared
libWPEWebKit-2.0.so) and the WPE backend is the WPEPlatform OpenHarmony
backend, which uses the WPEPlatform API rather than the legacy
`wpe_loader_interface` protocol — so nothing defines `_wpe_loader_interface`
and the final link fails with an undefined symbol.

The dlopen-based loader (src/loader.c) references the backend only by name
via dlsym at runtime, so it links cleanly and matches how a shared libwpe
behaves. Force it unconditionally.
---
 meson.build | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -99,7 +99,7 @@
 	'src/renderer-backend-egl.c',
 	'src/renderer-host.c',
 	'src/version.c',
 	'src/view-backend.c',
-	get_option('default_library') == 'shared' ? 'src/loader.c' : 'src/loader-static.c',
+	'src/loader.c',
 	install: true,
 	dependencies: dependencies,
 	version: soversion,
